00:29:15.880 --> 00:29:16.420
MELANIE WARRICK: Yeah.

00:29:16.420 --> 00:29:19.030
MARK MANDEL: So thanks out to
one of our community members,

00:29:19.030 --> 00:29:20.234
Justin Garrison.

00:29:20.234 --> 00:29:22.150
He sent in a wonderfully
interesting question,

00:29:22.150 --> 00:29:23.524
actually, that I
didn't even know

00:29:23.524 --> 00:29:24.790
existed, which was super cool.

00:29:24.790 --> 00:29:26.680
So the question
was basically, if I

00:29:26.680 --> 00:29:31.180
need to temporarily increase
the power of the Cloud Shell VM,

00:29:31.180 --> 00:29:32.310
how do I do that?

00:29:32.310 --> 00:29:34.422
So maybe I'm doing
some extra processing

00:29:34.422 --> 00:29:36.880
or I want to do something that's
computationally intensive,

00:29:36.880 --> 00:29:37.704
what do I do?

00:29:37.704 --> 00:29:40.120
MELANIE WARRICK: So there's a
boost mode that you can use.

00:29:40.120 --> 00:29:42.820
And that's something you can
find very easily in the Cloud

00:29:42.820 --> 00:29:43.900
Shell section.

00:29:43.900 --> 00:29:46.540
And so when you choose
that, it apparently

00:29:46.540 --> 00:29:49.360
will temporarily increase the
power of your Cloud Shell VM

00:29:49.360 --> 00:29:52.090
from a default G1
small machine type

00:29:52.090 --> 00:29:56.560
offering to an N1
standard one VM instance.

00:29:56.560 --> 00:29:58.240
So yeah, you just
press a button.

00:29:58.240 --> 00:29:59.930
MARK MANDEL: So like basically,
I'm going back to my childhood

00:29:59.930 --> 00:30:01.900
and remembering the turbo
button on my computer.

00:30:01.900 --> 00:30:02.775
MELANIE WARRICK: Yes.

00:30:06.350 --> 00:30:08.700
It feels like it should
be called turbo and red.

00:30:08.700 --> 00:30:09.450
MARK MANDEL: Yeah.

00:30:09.450 --> 00:30:10.151
Like totally.

00:30:10.151 --> 00:30:11.150
And you just left it on.

00:30:11.150 --> 00:30:12.233
Like I just left on turbo.

00:30:12.233 --> 00:30:14.460
Like I was ever like why
would you turn this off.

00:30:14.460 --> 00:30:16.190
It's worth noting
though, once activated,

00:30:16.190 --> 00:30:18.840
all sessions will be boosted
for the next 24 hours.

00:30:18.840 --> 00:30:21.236
And enabling boost mode will
restart your Cloud Shell

00:30:21.236 --> 00:30:22.860
and immediately
terminate your session.

00:30:22.860 --> 00:30:24.110
So just be prepared for that.

00:30:24.110 --> 00:30:25.440
It is an experimental feature.

00:30:25.440 --> 00:30:27.540
So additional limits may be
implemented in the future.

00:30:27.540 --> 00:30:29.910
But if you need that kind of
power it's there and available,

00:30:29.910 --> 00:30:30.620
which is kind of cool.

00:30:30.620 --> 00:30:31.610
MELANIE WARRICK:
Yes, definitely.

00:30:31.610 --> 00:30:32.450
MARK MANDEL: I love Cloud Shell.

00:30:32.450 --> 00:30:33.908
